ctor GateScanner Imaging Gateway GateScanner PE GateScanner Storebridge GateScanner Deep Detector TECHNOLOGY Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR) Why GateScanner ? CDR File Sanitization Samples LEARN Knowledge Base Blog Events News RESOURCES PRODUCTS – Latest Version log PRODUCT DATASHEETS VIDEOS CASE STUDIES DOCUMENTS & CERTIFICATIONS ABOUT US CONTACT US OUR TEAM CLIENTS TECHNOLOGY PARTNERS PARTNERS Multiscanning offline drives PRODUCTS GateScanner PE – Securing computing appliances GateScanner PE – bootable offline disk multi-scanning GateScanner PE performs entire HDD Multi-AV scans on MS Windows or Linux-based computing appliances and devices, including SCADA/ICS, aviation computers, drones, medical-imaging equipment and Point of Sale (POS) systems to ensure their integrity. Using WinPE technology, GateScanner PE is loaded pre-boot, gaining access to the entire hard disk drive – including protected sectors and BitLocker encrypted drives. Entire drives, or specified file paths can be scanned with up to six multiple AV’s, including NextGen AV’s, leading to a dramatic improvement in the level of malware detection. No software is installed and no files or configurations are altered, securing the device’s operational integrity. Any detected threats are flagged and their details logged for later treatment. A typical use case would be protecting a manufacturer’s production line from supply-chain attacks that could occur when machines are sent out for maintenance by third-party service providers. Upon their return, these appliances’ hard disks are deep-scanned for any malicious elements that may have been embedded on them off-site, prior to reconnecting them back to the production-floor network. The solution is delivered as a software application bundled with an isolable AV Updater and WIN PE ISO Creator applications for self-implementation on user-provided removable media, on vendor-supplied USB sticks, or in kiosk form with a Smart Touch screen*. * Regional availability may vary Supported file types: Windows: FAT16, FAT32, NTFS, ReFS, exFAT Apple: HFS, HFS+, APFS Linux: EXT2, EXT3, EXT4, XFS, ZFS, UFS2, ReiserFS, Reiser4, RomFS, Hikvision NAS and DVR FreeBSD/BSD: UFS2 General: RAID 0, 1, 4, 5, 50, 10, and JBOD DOWNLOAD Datasheet Try our award-winning solution today ! request a demo Twitter 27001 | 27032 | 27017 | 27018 | 9001 | 27799 | 90003 Solutions Secure Network separation Email security Secure Browsing Secure File Sharing Multi-site Network Protection real life use case technology Latest Releases Datasheets Videos Case Studies Certifications Legal Terms of use for cloud solutions END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT About Contact Us Our Team Clients Technology Partners Solutions Securer Network separation Email security Secure Browsing Secure File Sharing Multi-site Network Protection real life use case technology Latest Releases Datasheets Videos Case Studies Certifications About Contact Us Our Team Clients Technology_Partners Privacy Policy Copyright © 2026 – Sasa Software Privacy Policy Scroll to Top Scroll to Top",
