      "description": "What is Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR)? | Sasa Software Skip to content Solutions Close Solutions Open Solutions use cases Secure Network Segregation Email Security Secure Browsing Secure File Sharing Multi-Site Network Protection Real Life Use Cases products Security Dome Removable Media Kiosk Email Protection GateScanner Desktop [USB station] Integration Server [API] GateScanner Multi-source GS Injector [diode] Imaging Gateway GateScanner PE Storebridge [utility] GateScanner Deep Detector Technology Close Technology Open Technology TECHNOLOGY Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR) Why GateScanner ? CDR File Sanitization Samples RESOURCES Products - LATEST RELEASES Product Datasheets Videos Case Studies Documents & Certifications About Close About Open About SASA SOFTWARE Contact Us Our Team Clients Technology Partners Careers Partners To Japanese Website Learn Close Learn Open Learn KNOWLEDGE Knowledge Base Blog: Inside Talk NEWS & EVENTS News Events Support Book a Demo SOLUTIONS Secure Network Segregation Email Security Secure Browsing Secure File Sharing Multi-Site Network Protection Real Life Use Cases PRODUCTS GateScanner Security Dome Removable Media Kiosk Email protection Desktop Kiosk GateScanner Integration Server GateScanner Multi-source GateScanner Injector GateScanner Imaging Gateway GateScanner PE GateScanner Storebridge GateScanner Deep Detector TECHNOLOGY Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR) Why GateScanner ? CDR File Sanitization Samples LEARN Knowledge Base Blog Events News RESOURCES PRODUCTS – Latest Version log PRODUCT DATASHEETS VIDEOS CASE STUDIES DOCUMENTS & CERTIFICATIONS ABOUT US CONTACT US OUR TEAM CLIENTS TECHNOLOGY PARTNERS PARTNERS SOLUTIONS Secure Network Segregation Email Security Secure Browsing Secure File Sharing Multi-Site Network Protection Real Life Use Cases PRODUCTS GateScanner Security Dome Removable Media Kiosk Email protection Desktop Kiosk GateScanner Integration Server GateScanner Multi-source GateScanner Injector GateScanner Imaging Gateway GateScanner PE GateScanner Storebridge GateScanner Deep Detector TECHNOLOGY Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR) Why GateScanner ? CDR File Sanitization Samples LEARN Knowledge Base Blog Events News RESOURCES PRODUCTS – Latest Version log PRODUCT DATASHEETS VIDEOS CASE STUDIES DOCUMENTS & CERTIFICATIONS ABOUT US CONTACT US OUR TEAM CLIENTS TECHNOLOGY PARTNERS PARTNERS Content Disarm Reconstruction Cdr: Secure Your Digital Infrastructure Content Disarm and Reconstruction Technology (CDR) WHAT IS CONTENT DISARM AND RECONSTRUCTION (CDR) TECHNOLOGY? Also known as ‘file sanitization’ or ‘content sanitization’ – Content Disarm and Reconstruction (CDR) is an advanced anti-malware technology providing superior results in the prevention of file-based attacks – effectively blocking the initial access phase of most APT’s, ransomware and zero-day attacks. CDR generates for each incoming email and file – a functionally-equivalent copy that is devoid of any malicious content, and does it in near real-time. A major benefit of CDR is that it does not rely on detection to eliminate threats, making it the tool of choice for defence from unknown, zero-day malware. In addition, it greatly minimizes reliance on user judgement and compliance, since all incoming content is disarmed prior to arriving at the endpoints. How DOES CONTENT DISARM AND RECONSTRUCTION (CDR) TECHNOLOGY WORK? Content Disarm and Reconstruction dissects each incoming (or outgoing) file to its most elementary components and scans them with NextGen AI, and multiple AV engines, achieving superior detection results. It then proceeds to reconstitute the files and emails, in strict adherence to vendor specifications, disrupting, in process, any remaining unknown (‘signature-less’) malware that may have passed through undetected (see our ‘ Before & After CDR Processing ‘ samples page ). A good CDR solution is marked by its deep deconstruction/reconstitution process, and its high-throughput capacity. Content Disarm and Reconstruction stages 1. File or Email is deconstructed to its elementary components and scanned for threats, and appropriate mitigations applied to each component separately. In the case of GateScanner, these include multi file-type verifications, multi-AV scans, static code analysis on binary segments with the optional disabling of active components such as macros and embedded scripts according to pre-defined security profiles. 2. File or Email is then reconstructed through transformations to remove any remaining unknown/undetected malicious code, foreign to the vendor-specified format. Why GateScanner? Excellence . We are certain that our CDR technology is practically impregnable. Our clients’ independent penetration tests repeatedly show up to 99.99 % success rates in the obstruction of unknown, file-borne threats – and that’s the bottom line, but that’s not the whole story… Modularity and Scalability . Adding a new component to an existing system can be a major challenge. Flexibility is key to a successful implementation. With this in mind, we’ve built GateScanner to be modular, highly configurable and easily scalable with zero-downtime on-prem scalability. Pick and choose any part of the CDR process that you wish to apply, select which channels to protect, and chain up to ten GateScanner engines on-the-fly, to achieve virtually unlimited processing capacity. Easily Integrated . Challenged to deliver unique solutions for a wide variety of client configurations, GateScanner features a unique external-tools integration engine that enables IT security teams to insert CDR content sanitization at any point along the data flow, before or after existing security tools, significantly upgrading the network’s security profile. Customizable. For us, every client is an opportunity to get creative. Our highly dedicated development team works closely with each client to fulfill their most ambitious goals. We look forward to tailor your solution!",
